# Build trees.
#
# Every component is configured out-of-source, and between them they use a
# dozen names: `build` for the lab build, plus `build-clean`, `build-ubtrap`,
# `build-rel`, `build-verify`, `build-cmake` and `cmake-build` for the
# sanitizer, measured and verification configurations. The glob covers the ones
# that exist and the ones the next configuration will invent. Together they are
# most of this tree by size.
build/
build-*/
cmake-build*/

# Compiler and linker output, wherever it lands.
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Runtime state. P01, P02 and P06 each own a SQLite database and P05 an
# append-only journal; all four are produced by a run and none describes the
# source. The lock and sidecar files go with them.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.lock
*.journal
var/
state/

# Test verdicts and benchmark manifests are results, not sources, and a stale
# one is worse than none: it names a run on a host that no longer exists.
test-artifacts/
reports/manifest-*.json

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
